  "question": {
    "text": "A body of density $1.2 \\times 10^{3} \\mathrm{~kg} / \\mathrm{m}^{3}$ is dropped from rest from a height $1 \\mathrm{~m}$ into a liquid of density $2.4 \\times 10^{3} \\mathrm{~kg} / \\mathrm{m}^{3}$. Neglecting all dissipative effects, the maximum depth to which the body sinks before returning to float on the surface is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "gsTZf",
      "text": "$0.1 \\mathrm{~m}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28a7O",
      "text": "$1 \\mathrm{~m}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "yOU2B",
      "text": "$0.01 \\mathrm{~m}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "4hhGo",
      "text": "$2 \\mathrm{~m}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{d}=1.2 \\times 10^{3}, \\mathrm{~h}=1 \\mathrm{~m}, \\rho=2.4 \\times 10^{3}$\r\nBy work Energy Theorem,\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\n\\mathrm{Mg}(\\mathrm{h}+\\mathrm{d})=\\mathrm{Bd} \\\\\r\n\\mathrm{V}\\left(1.2 \\times 10^{-3}\\right) \\mathrm{g}(1+\\mathrm{d})=\\mathrm{V}\\left(2.4 \\times 10^{-3}\\right) \\mathrm{g} \\mathrm{d} \\\\\r\n\\therefore \\mathrm{d}=1 \\mathrm{~m}\r\n\\end{array}\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
